Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: When are representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.4 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer. The obligations of Acquirer to complete the acquisition are subject to the fulfillment or waiver by Acquirer at or prior to the Closing Date of the following conditions: (a) each of the representations and warranties of the Target contained in this Agreement shall be true and correct in all material respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date, except where the failure to be true and correct would not reasonably be expected to have a Material Adverse Effect; provided, however, that any representation or warranty that is expressly stated to be made as of a specific date shall be true and correct as of such specific date. Additionally, the representations and warranties in Sections 4.1 and 4.3 must be true and correct in all respects as of the date hereof and the Closing Date, without regard to materiality. (Page 92)
